course: dictionary
lesson: 6974
title: Panic and staying calm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Panic is a sudden, very strong fear. It can make you stop thinking clearly and act wildly. Read the sentence around the word to understand it. «Her mum arrived late and panicked» tells you that the mum was very frightened and could not think clearly.
explain: The word panic is also a verb. To panic means to feel this fear and act without thinking. Look at the clues. In «a last-minute panic», there is little time left, so the word means being in a great hurry and worry.
explain: Panic is often the wrong reaction in an emergency. Staying calm and following a plan usually helps more than running about. When you feel panic rising, breathe slowly and think about what to do next.
fact: Panic means a sudden, very strong fear that stops you thinking clearly.
fact: To panic means to feel this fear and act without thinking.
fact: «In a panic» can mean in a great hurry and worry, as in «a last-minute panic».
fact: In an emergency, staying calm and following a plan usually helps more than running about.
fact: Breathing slowly can help stop panic.
exercise: «Her mum arrived late and panicked.» What does panicked mean here? | *Felt sudden, strong fear and stopped thinking clearly | Smiled and sang a song | Went to sleep early | Ate a big dinner slowly
exercise: «A last-minute panic» means what? | A slow, happy breakfast | A long, quiet holiday | A calm walk in the park | *A rush of worry because there is little time left
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the opposite of panic in this sentence: «Stay calm and follow the plan.» | *calm | stay | follow | plan
test: What is a panic? | A kind of musical instrument | A happy party with music | *A sudden, very strong fear that stops clear thinking | A long, slow walk
test: What does it mean to panic? | To sing a song loudly | To sit quietly and read a book | *To feel sudden fear and act without thinking | To plan a party carefully
exam: In an emergency, why is staying calm better than panicking? | Panic makes the danger smaller | Shouting loudly makes you calmer | *Staying calm and following a plan helps more than running about | Running about wildly helps you find the way out
